# What NOT to upload to Cloud Build.
#
# The presence of this file switches gcloud off its default, which is to read
# .gitignore. That default would have uploaded tests/, docs/, data/ and
# frameworks/ — none of which the image copies — and skipped nothing that
# matters. The list below is therefore the whole exclusion policy, not an
# addition to .gitignore.

.git/
.gitignore
.superpowers/
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Not copied by the Dockerfile. The generated parquet under data/ is the
# largest thing in the tree and the screens read none of it at runtime: the
# figures they show were baked into apps/shared/data/ by
# scripts/build_app_data.py before the commit.
#
# EVERY ONE OF THESE IS ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, and that is not tidiness.
# These patterns follow .gitignore semantics, where a bare `data/` matches a
# directory of that name at ANY depth. Written bare, it excluded
# apps/shared/data/ — the entire figures bundle every screen in both
# applications reads — and the first deployed revision served ten pages that
# each 404'd on bundle.js.
/data/
/docs/
/frameworks/
/packages/
/tests/
/agent_manifest.json
